  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Primary Health Care provision for vulnerable populations affected by food insecurity and malnutrition in Blue Nile and other conflict-affected states with high IDP populations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;overall objective&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt; aims to contribute to improve the health conditions of vulnerable populations affected by extreme poverty, food insecurity and malnutrition in Sudan including host communities, Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) and refugees. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;specific objective&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt; is to increase sustainable access to and demand for quality Primary Health Care (PHC), Nutrition and Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) services in Blue Nile and other conflict-affected states, including for host communities, IDPs and refugees.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
